.title openEMS comparison: as built: Compact Wilkinson, 1 section, f0 = 2.4 GHz on jlc-ro4350b-1.524 (arms modelled as coupled pairs)
# substrate jlc-ro4350b-1.524; arms as coupled pairs (Kirschning–Jansen) at a 1 mm gap; 0603 resistors bridging it
# sections: W 2.781 mm, 19.52 mm, R 73.33 Ω; outputs at a 12 mm pitch through two mitred bends each
# lossless, 2.16–2.64 GHz: return loss ≥ 20.4 dB (input), ≥ 24.4 dB (outputs); isolation ≥ 21 dB; split -3.05 … -3.011 dB
# not modelled: the junction where the input line meets both arms; the resistor body over the gap (its pads, ESL and body capacitance are)
.freq 1200000000 3600000000 401
.ref 2400000000
.substrate jlc-ro4350b-1.524
# ports at the openEMS measurement planes (the feeds shortened by 6.072000000000001/6.072000000000003/6.072000000000003 mm); the openEMS result overlays every S trace
.data em wilkinson-2g4-ro4350b-1524-openems.s3p overlay
.param s = 1mm   # gap between the arms (the resistor bridges it)
.param wf = 3.29115mm   # port lines (50 ohm)
.param w1 = 2.781385mm tune 1.947mm 3.8939mm
.param l1 = 19.51597mm tune 15.613mm 23.419mm
.param r1 = 73.3333 tune 36.667 146.67
port in 50
port o1 50
port o2 50
To2_f o2 o2_k W=3.2912mm len=0.5mm
To1_f o1 o1_k W=3.2912mm len=0.5mm
Tin_f in in_k W=3.2912mm len=2.4456mm
cline K1 geom=msl W=w1 S=s
  len l1
  A in_k in_k
  B a1 b1
end
res R1 a1 b1 R=r1 pkg=0603 esl=0 cp=0
TOa_1 a1 Oa_1e W=3.29115mm len=4.936724mm
bend Oa_B1 Oa_1e Oa_2s W=3.29115mm mitre=opt
TOa_2 Oa_2s Oa_2e W=3.29115mm len=0.563276mm
bend Oa_B2 Oa_2e Oa_3s W=3.29115mm mitre=opt
TOa_3 Oa_3s o1_k W=3.29115mm len=4.936724mm
TOb_1 b1 Ob_1e W=3.29115mm len=4.936724mm
bend Ob_B1 Ob_1e Ob_2s W=3.29115mm mitre=opt
TOb_2 Ob_2s Ob_2e W=3.29115mm len=0.563276mm
bend Ob_B2 Ob_2e Ob_3s W=3.29115mm mitre=opt
TOb_3 Ob_3s o2_k W=3.29115mm len=4.936724mm
.goal db(S11) < -20 2160000000 2640000000
.goal db(S22) < -20 2160000000 2640000000
.goal db(S32) < -20 2160000000 2640000000
.plot ylim=-50,0 db(S11) db(S21) db(S31) db(S22) db(S32)

